.TH geectl-changelog-identity 1  "geectl-changelog-identity 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-changelog\-identity \- Print the resolved `.changes` entry author in `Name <email>` form — the same value a bare `changelog generate` would write. The author resolves through the identity chain (#405): config `[identity]`, then `VC_REALNAME` / `VC_MAILADDR`, then the OBS account, then git identity; the command refuses when none yields an identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl changelog identity\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIDIR\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the resolved `.changes` entry author in `Name <email>` form — the same value a bare `changelog generate` would write. The author resolves through the identity chain (#405): config `[identity]`, then `VC_REALNAME` / `VC_MAILADDR`, then the OBS account, then git identity; the command refuses when none yields an identity
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR] [default: .]
The package directory (default: the current directory). The git level reads identity from here
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
